{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Not because of your righteousness do you come to possess.</b> For indeed, the fact that you inherit the land is not on your merit, so that it would not be fitting for YHWH to fight on your behalf in order that you may possess it swiftly." "<b>But because of the wickedness of these nations YHWH your Elohim dispossesses them from before you.</b> That He desired their punishment to come through you — that you would destroy them for their iniquity, as it says: וַיֹּאמֶר הַשְׁמֵד (Deuteronomy 33:27), in contrast to וּבְיַד אָדָם אַל אֶפֹּלָה (II Samuel 24:14)." "<b>And in order to establish.</b> And so that through the fulfillment of His commandment you may merit to possess it, in the manner of כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר בִּלְבָבִי עָשִׂיתָ לְבֵית אַחְאָב, בְּנֵי רְבִעִים יֵשְׁבוּ לְךָ עַל כִּסֵּא יִשְׂרָאֵל (II Kings 10:30). And all this He did in order to establish what He swore to the fathers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "The verse cited as Deuteronomy 33:27 reads וַיֹּאמֶר הַשְׁמֵד, which does not match the Masoretic text of that verse; rendered as Sforno quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:01.917015669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}